  "cues": [
   [
    0.117,
    "Back to the sugar chains, because they carry the identity badge."
   ],
   [
    4.076,
    "Cells recognise each other by binding to molecules on their surface, often carbohydrates."
   ],
   [
    10.078,
    "Each chain is covalently bonded to something in the membrane."
   ],
   [
    14.219,
    "If it is bonded to a lipid, we call it a glycolipid."
   ],
   [
    17.643,
    "If it is bonded to a protein, a glycoprotein, and that is the more common kind."
   ],
   [
    22.956,
    "They sit only on the external side of the membrane, facing outward, where other cells can touch them."
   ],
   [
    29.284,
    "And the chains differ."
   ],
   [
    30.573,
    "They vary from species to species, from one individual to another, and even between different types of cells in the same body."
   ],
   [
    38.711,
    "That variety is what makes them useful as badges."
   ],
   [
    41.992,
    "So cells can tell who is who."
   ]
  ]
 },
